The Group’s risk profile can be summarised as follows: 

The two main types of risks that the Group needs to manage are asset liability management risks 
and technical risks. 
(a) Asset liability management risks 
Risks linked to asset liability management arise mainly in the life insurance savings business. 
The Group performs regular asset-liability matching reviews to measure and manage the financial 
risks, based on medium and/or long-term income statement and balance sheet projections prepared 
according to various economic scenarios. 
The main financial risks linked to asset liability management fall into five categories: 
▪ risks of an increase and decrease of the interest rates;  
▪ risks linked to the decrease of equity and real estate markets;
